 "bout_definition": "A bout is a maximal run of True in the loader's per-fly mask (eval/flies_extract.py masks_from_actions then runs), per behavior and per fly: actions.mat [start, end] (MATLAB 1-based inclusive) becomes python [start-1, end); overlapping or touching raw rows of the same fly and behavior merge into one run. Lunge and wing_threat are counted separately, fly 0 and fly 1 separately (both flies counted). Runs are taken over the full movie, so a bout already running at frame 22500 keeps its true onset and is not counted. Minimum length: none; the scorer (eval/flies_score.py _kept_runs) uses none and only drops a bout whose every frame is excluded (either fly 'unknown'); that drop is applied here. The onset is the run's first python frame.",
